   "text": {
    "L1": "Road safety means using rules that protect people walking and travelling.",
    "L2": "Walk on the footpath, and cross at the zebra crossing.",
    "L3": "Before crossing, look right, look left, and look right again.",
    "L4": "Red means stop, yellow means get ready, and green means go.",
    "L5": "Always wear a helmet on a scooter and a seat belt in a car.",
    "L6": "Here is a mistake: “Not cross the road here.” We say, “Don't cross the road here.”",
    "L7": "If a ball rolls onto the road, do not run after it. Stay on the footpath and ask an adult.",
    "L8": "Now put the three crossing actions in the correct order."
   },
